{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790283330,"nonce":"k7WBSAiSwnFKLg7nOo7YFnerTcA=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis), later the same day as comment #2, which this supersedes on the wire form. Design: doc/design/terminal-renderer.md.\n\nThe spec is gone. A view's input is one KWARGS object, the same object work.view.KIND(**kwargs) takes, so the command already is the serialization and there is nothing named {\"view\",\"bindings\",\"items\"} left to send. --gui is therefore the only gui switch, on `view` and on `flow run`, and the wire form to the gui is that KWARGS object. Nothing prints a spec any more: `git work view` has no --format, no TTY and no --gui is an error, and an agent that wants data runs `git work issue PROGRAM` rather than opening a view headlessly.\n\nUnchanged: `gui` stays the HTTP surface, runs flows in its own process, selects an HTML backend for the very same work.view.* calls the terminal renders, and a backend missing a view kind fails naming itself. The rename webui -\u003e gui, with no `tui` command, is untouched.","files":null}]}